    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0590" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/2838: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-24T18:00:00-03:00">March 24, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1117. Reference final paragraph Department’s 950, March 22, 9 p.m.<anchor n="75"
                        xml:id="d543-f1"/> The need for commercial trucks to transport foodstuffs,
                    fuel and other products essential to Brazil’s economy is of major importance to
                    Brazil. The situation has changed materially, since our A–530, March 23,
                        1943,<anchor n="76" xml:id="d543-f2"/> and Brazil will need at least 2,637
                    trucks and other commodities resulting from inadequate transportation
                    facilities. It is also of the greatest importance that Brazil receive as quickly
                    as possible the spare parts ordered by preference requests now on file in
                    Washington.</p>
                <p>The Brazilian Government has signified its intention to ration the trucks in
                    Brazil in accordance with the conditions established in the United States by
                    General Conservation Order M–100<anchor n="77" xml:id="d543-f3"/> and its
                    amendments (see Embassy’s despatch 15045, March 22<anchor n="78"
                        xml:id="d543-f4"/>).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d543-f1" n="75" xml:id="d543-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning this agreement, see <ref target="#pg543">pp.
                        543</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d543-f2" n="76" xml:id="d543-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d543-f3" n="77" xml:id="d543-f3-content">
                <p>An order which established the rationing, among other things, of trucks and
                    trailers in the United States.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d543-f4" n="78" xml:id="d543-f4-content">
                <p>Despatch not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
